<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n106696" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑμέτερος</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ῡ]</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, 
			Dor.
		 and 
			Ep.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑμός</span></b>  (q.v.): (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑμεῖς</span>):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>your, yours,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i>, etc.; with a Pron. added in gen., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑμέτερος ἑκάστου θυμός</span> the courage <i>of</i>
			each of <i>you,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				17.226
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑμέτερος θυμὸς αὐτῶν</span>
			<i>your</i> own mind, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				2.138
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑμέτερόνδε</span>”
				<i>to your house,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					23.86
				</span></i>
			: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ὑ.</span>
			<i>your part, your business,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἢν μὴ τὸ ὑ. αἴτιον γένηται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					8.140
				</span></i>
			.<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ά</span>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Grg.</u>
				522c
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ δ᾽ ὑ. πρᾶξαι</span>
			<i>your character</i> is to . . , <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				1.70
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ ὑ.</span>”
				<i>your goods,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Cyr.</u>
					3.2.12
				</span></i>
			: in Prose sts. with the Article, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταῖς ὑμετέραις πόλεσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					836c
				</span></i>
			; and objectively, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱ ὑ
			ἐλπίδες</span> hopes <i>raised by you,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				1.69
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ τῇ ὑ.
			παρακελεύσει</span> for the purpose of advising <i>you,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Ap.</u>
				36d
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> poet.
			(never in 
				Att.
			) sts. for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σός,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Sol.
				19.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Del.</u>
				204
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				227
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Nonn.
				<u>D.</u>
				5.340
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				5.292
			</span></i> (Paul. Sil.).</div>
